Subject: MSstats removes features with few measurements although removeFewMeasurements is set to False
Message-ID: <p018V5WZGLk.MlQrRcrEAQAJ@msstats.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/msstats/c/p018V5WZGLk/m/MlQrRcrEAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi, I noticed that OpenMStoMSstatsFormat and dataProcess remove features with few measurements (in less than 3 runs) although the option is set to False. I have 3 replicates per condition so I want to keep features present in 2 runs. I am working with the output of quantms and MSstats v4.8.2
When reading the input file prior to MSstats I see features present in 1 or 2 runs.

> data <- read.csv("secretome/quantms/noMBR/proteomicslfq/sdrf_openms_design_msstats_in.csv", header = TRUE, sep = ',')
> data %>% group_by(PeptideSequence, PrecursorCharge) %>% summarise(RunCount = sum(!is.na <http://is.na>(Intensity))) %>% ungroup() %>% count(RunCount) %>% mutate(Frequency = n / sum(n))
`summarise()` has grouped output by 'PeptideSequence'. You can override using the `.groups` argument.
# A tibble: 6 × 3
RunCount n Frequency
<int> <int> <dbl>
1 1 2000 0.380
2 2 978 0.186
3 3 125 0.0237
4 4 374 0.0710
5 5 659 0.125
6 6 1128 0.214

Now if I read this in msstats

> data_msstats <- OpenMStoMSstatsFormat(data, useUniquePeptide = TRUE, removeFewMeasurements=FALSE, removeProtein_with1Feature = FALSE, +  summaryforMultipleRows = max, use_log_file = FALSE)
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:34] ** Raw data from OpenMS imported successfully.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:36] ** Raw data from OpenMS cleaned successfully.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:36] ** Using annotation extracted from quantification data. INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:36] ** Run labels were standardized to remove symbols such as '.' or '%'.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:36] ** The following options are used:
- Features will be defined by the columns: PeptideSequence, PrecursorCharge, FragmentIon, ProductCharge
- Shared peptides will be removed.
- Proteins with single feature will not be removed
. - Features with less than 3 measurements across runs will be kept.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Features with all missing measurements across runs are removed.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Shared peptides are removed.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Multiple measurements in a feature and a run are summarized by summaryforMultipleRows: max
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Features with all missing measurements across runs are removed.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Run annotation merged with quantification data. INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Features with one or two measurements across runs are removed.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Fractionation handled.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:38] ** Updated quantification data to make balanced design. Missing values are marked by NA INFO [2023-06-02 12:32:38] ** Finished preprocessing. The dataset is ready to be processed by the dataProcess function.
> data_msstats %>% group_by(PeptideSequence, PrecursorCharge) %>% summarise(RunCount = sum(!is.na <http://is.na>(Intensity))) %>% ungroup() %>% count(RunCount) %>% mutate(Frequency = n / sum(n))
`summarise()` has grouped output by 'PeptideSequence'. You can override using the `.groups` argument.
