3 5 659 0.288
4 6 1128 0.493

So MSstats only kept features present in >3 runs. The log output says first that
Features with less than 3 measurements across runs will be kept.
and then
INFO  [2023-06-02 12:32:37] ** Features with one or two measurements across runs are removed.

I tried the dataProcess function giving as input the data and not the data_msstats dataframe but the same filtering is applied again and prints that these features are removed.

> processed.quant <- MSstats::dataProcess(raw = data, +  normalization = "equalizeMedians", +  featureSubset = "all", +  summaryMethod = 'TMP', +  censoredInt = "NA", +  MBimpute = TRUE, +  use_log_file = FALSE)
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Features with one or two measurements across runs are removed.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Fractionation handled.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Updated quantification data to make balanced design. Missing values are marked by NA
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Log2 intensities under cutoff = 15.542 were considered as censored missing values.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Log2 intensities = NA were considered as censored missing values.
INFO [2023-06-02 12:35:40] ** Use all features that the dataset originally has.

Checked again that there are no proteins with more than 3 missing values (I have 6 samples in total).
> sampleQuant <- quantification(processed.quant, use_log_file = FALSE)
> table(rowSums(is.na <http://is.na>(sampleQuant[, 2:7])))
0   1   2   3
416 112  69  28

